# Amendment 1.0.6: land finite routing admission and search separately

The next geometry prerequisite for the real UI composition is a bounded router over landed U10b placements. Legacy F17/#36 supplies a proposed Rust algorithm, not an ELK translation. Its 403 production lines exceed the ordinary cap before factoring; the complete original routing test file contains 439 lines and 16 tests. This amendment assigns U11a admission, then U11b search. Forest admission/placement and the fractional caller bridge require separate future scope review.

## Preserve the original source and tests

The donor `syson-routing/src/lib.rs` is SHA-256 `4ef440f6c241ce7e008b679e0781e65a9df03861b625fae3349343f3782c5c0e`; `tests/routing.rs` is `2f84297784fd60b6dbe18e6842f45f196c6d11866cad11cdb09d246af5006ec6`. U11a receives lines 1–117, 123–174, 185–194 and 209–270 (241 lines; assigned-byte hash `f5467b1e7c48ba504cdd68d8c8f0458df12552f67f36560fd210d5d45e14504d`). U11b receives 118–122, 175–184, 195–208 and 271–403 (162 lines; `0ade8658655a992e3ff73da65243ec4628784cdbd0e280d913abac5edb9ed6bf`). Search-only push/collision helpers belong to U11b; U11a must qualify without unused private helpers or added public surface. Every source line is assigned once. Preserve all 16 original tests byte-for-byte on the final public wrapper; add admission/continuation regressions separately.

U10b is actually landed at `974e7591ec4296db96644954edb4d4daf71f41d6`, crate tree `fa12c1312c969adac6f9d30cffe130dec36a28f7`, placement SHA-256 `cd5de614196e30f55082c0ec68ffe9680936678dde19e3f5faa141fb2bbcfb01`. Its 26 composed tests and published finite measurements do not accept native/UI geometry. Bind these actual public types; do not restore obsolete private U10 helpers.

## U11a: admit canonical integer routing inputs

Preserve Point/Side/Edge/Limits/typed errors, exact doubled integer coordinates and the original defaults: 128 nodes, 256 edges, 16,384 grid vertices, 65,536 output points, 20,000,000 work and 1,024 ID bytes. Validate IDs/endpoints, integer positive rectangles and bounds, overlapping interiors and side-center terminals through checked arithmetic and fallible buffers. Retain fractional/nonfinite/degenerate refusal; side selection constrains anchor position, not departure heading.

Admission produces an opaque prepared-routing token with immutable canonical geometry/terminals, its own original callback and accumulated spent work. Keep guard construction/reset and independent graph/guard recombination private. Search consumes the token once without recopying/resorting admission or replacing its guard. Exact/over limits, permutations, unchanged inputs and early/interior cancellation need public API tests. Logical charges/reservations are neither an RSS bound nor a deadline.

## U11b: consume admission and publish routes atomically

After reviewed U11a is on main and locally qualified, pin its exact bytes and implement the visibility grid, blocked-cell tests, hop-minimizing BFS, simplification and canonical result. Preserve `route(nodes,edges,limits,cancelled)`, all original result fields, coincident parallel routes and zero-clearance boundary/corner contact. Preserve checked grid/output arithmetic, initial/phase/late cancellation and final publication polling, including empty-edge success. Failure returns no partial result.

Run the complete 16-test file plus admission tests. Add actual admit→search spent-work/callback continuation controls, including a budget that admits either phase alone but refuses their combined work, cancellation between phases and late publication cancellation. A type/token inspection alone is insufficient. Keep resource qualification in a separately sized development-tool PR if needed.

## Dependencies, budgets and remaining acceptance

The finite chain is landed U10b → U11a → U11b. U11 retains its original U10 prerequisite, tasks, source paths and all native/fractional/UI gates; add U11b to implementation readiness and both accepted children to parent acceptance. Full U10/U11 feature acceptance is not a finite child's source prerequisite. This amendment grants no source or runtime lease and releases no held registration.

U11a targets at most 360 changed production/700 authored lines; U11b targets 270/860 including all 439 original test lines. Hard caps remain 400 changed handwritten production and 900 authored lines, additions plus deletions after ordinary formatting, including helpers/imports/tests/manifests/notices/coordinator wiring. Adopt another meaningful split before coding if required; never compress source or drop tests to fit. Coordinator owns crate exports, manifest/lock, notices and application assembly; child module leases remain separate and sequential.

Profile named ordinary 32/64-node fixtures and bounded 128/256/1024 ramps under unchanged defaults, with realistic IDs, two warmups/seven measured ranges and separate work, allocation/live-heap/RSS metrics. Above 128 nodes the default router refuses Nodes; refusal latency is not capacity. Thirty measured samples plus a declared estimator are required for p95. Existing workload-specific performance ranges remain unchanged.

The integer router does not consume every valid f64 measurement/layout result. Keep original refusal tests and the real #130 ceil/fractional refusal/conversion evidence. A future matched native numeric policy must qualify 97.125-sized leaves, fractional headers/gaps/borders/retained positions, signed zero, nonfinite/overflow/precision cases and attached endpoints without silent quantization. Nested routing, constrained ports, manual bends, reconnect semantics, worker/stale results/history, actual font measurement and native rendered readability remain parent work. Actual UI qualification still requires pointer/keyboard cancellation, focus/selection, undo/reload and 320/1440 px plus 200/400% zoom. No old #130 result transfers automatically.

Contract 1.0.6 has 788 review units: every prior 786 plus U11a/U11b. Preserve all 55 historical records, existing policy objects, prior amendments, ownership holds and performance requirements. The typed routing policy validates before its two IDs may be excluded from older inventories; missing policy/children, coherently dropped edges, wider caps/scope and lost original tests/source/parent gates must refuse under normal and optimized Python. Static integrity does not establish runtime or feature acceptance.

The complete verifier reconstructs all 786 original normalized records and checks their retained hash. Restore only U11 delegation, C99's new child dependencies and the two derived routing inputs in C04/C08/C09; preserve every other field and record order. Those joint gates retain both new implementation inputs in the current graph. Run this whole-record proof after the existing diagnostic guards, so their original refusal controls retain precise outcomes.
